          "line": 254
        },
        {
          "path": "Modules/Services/SelfRenewal/SelfRenewalSigningMaterialVault.swift",
          "line": 357
        }
      ],
      "assessment": "The real current key creates a signed CSR; the returned certificate candidate must match its public hash. The account/team and actual persisted key/generation are checked again after network awaits. Only the original Vault publish performs final chain/date/key/profile CMS/group/identity validation and publication CAS. A retained CSR or token does not bypass the current Vault; stale/revoked/observed cancellation remains rejected before commit."
    },
    {
      "concern": "Committed publication is not mistaken for rollback",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "path": ".build/renewal-discovery/account-enrollment-step/final-sources/Modules/Services/SelfRenewal/SelfRenewalDeveloperAccountClient.swift",
          "line": 261
        },
        {
          "path": ".build/renewal-discovery/account-enrollment-step/final-sources/Modules/Services/SelfRenewal/SelfRenewalDeveloperAccountClient.swift",
          "line": 281
        },
        {
          "path": "Modules/Services/SelfRenewal/SelfRenewalSigningMaterialVault.swift",
          "line": 452
        }
      ],
      "assessment": "After acknowledged Vault publication, the later account save can fail or notice cancellation but returns PublicationFinalizationFailure carrying the actual lease. Finalization re-reads the original Vault and requires exact key, generation+1 and actual leaf digest, then clears intent without another remote request. No post-commit cancellation check discards the commit fact. Concurrent later Vault changes can conservatively prevent finalization; there is no claim of cross-owner atomicity."
    },
